            <div xml:id="d382">

                <pb facs="0452" n="434" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg434"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.24532/1–3046: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Berle</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-02-04T19:00:00-05:00">February 4, 1946—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>176. Urtel 207 Jan 30.<anchor n="15"
                        xml:id="d382-f1"/> Dept is actively pursuing subject of air base
                    installations. Commitment to turn installations over to Brazilian Govt now
                    admitted by FLC as well as War Dept but channels
                    and mechanics still to be worked out. Instructions will be sent as soon as
                    possible. Temporary delivery of custody suggested urtel undesirable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
